Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7603: defer watchdog work after a channel error

The core holds dev->mutex while calling the driver's set_channel callback.
Calling mt7603_mac_work() directly after an MCU channel-switch error tries
to acquire that same mutex again and blocks the caller indefinitely.

Queue the watchdog work immediately instead. It can acquire the mutex after
the callback returns and the core releases it. A timeout already raises
mcu_hang to the watchdog threshold, so the queued work can perform
recovery.

Fixes: f4fdd7716290 ("wifi: mt76: partially move channel change code to core")
Assisted-by: LLM
---
--- a/mt7603/main.c
+++ b/mt7603/main.c
@@ -197,7 +197,7 @@
 	tasklet_enable(&dev->mt76.pre_tbtt_tasklet);
 
 	if (failed)
-		mt7603_mac_work(&dev->mphy.mac_work.work);
+		ieee80211_queue_delayed_work(mt76_hw(dev), &dev->mphy.mac_work, 0);
 
 	return ret;
 }
